module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: in the v1 seed, three independent non-rejections let a wrong-typed value stand where a declared type is required, with ZERO blocking diagnostics. (A) `Present { value: <record R> }` returned from a fn declared `-> T?` where T is a coproduct. (B) a bare record R returned from a fn declared `-> T` where T is a coproduct. (C) `==` between operands of unrelated types, a coproduct field against its own row and two unrelated records. Each is accepted; the positive control (`Present { value: r.arch }`, `r.arch == a`) is accepted too, so the acceptance is a missing judgment and not a blanket. A bare record at `T?` IS refused (declared Optional<Arch>, produced Row), which locates (A) at the Optional wrapper.",

    "SPECIMEN (snappy-seal-211, gunbc#14063 before 20d205c7529, in-tree RED at e5d277c5c42): extdeps.cpu.types soc_family_architecture was declared `-> Architecture?`, took `lead`, the first CpuModelCatalogRow of the family, compared `m.architecture == lead` (field against row: always false) and returned `Present { value: lead }` (a row where an Architecture was declared). v2-bootstrap was green. HARM: every SoC family established no architecture, which silently emptied the reset roster. A SILENT WRONG ANSWER, DESIGN section 5, outside the ladder. It was found by a reviewer reading the fold, not by any gate.",

    "THE CHAIN, DESIGN section 6b. The two declared-type judgments are split. `declared_type_conformance_diags_core` (src/v1/04_infer.dag), the one the declared-return and data-initializer positions consult, has no arm for a product at a declared coproduct, so (B) falls through; `product_versus_coproduct_head_mismatch` exists but is reached only from `declared_type_inhabitance`. That judgment answers UndecidableOptionalCarrier whenever EITHER side is optional, and never compares the Optional payloads, so (A) abstains exactly where the payload is the whole question. For (C) the comparison operands are not judged against each other in the seed. Earliest unjustified boundary: the declared-type obligation abstaining on the Optional payload and on the product-versus-coproduct head, not the fn that returned the row.",

    "SAME CLASS AS THE BallGridArray PROBE (extdeps.cpu.types, comment on SocketTermination)? SAME FAMILY, DIFFERENT HOLE. Both are the checker resolving or accepting a value without testing it against the declared coproduct it must inhabit, and both were found in extdeps.cpu.types. BallGridArray is a bare VARIANT NAME resolved from the pool and never tested for membership in the declared coproduct (a wrong arm of the right type, stored or compared, never matched). This one is a whole RECORD VALUE of the wrong type escaping a declared Optional or coproduct return, plus a cross-type `==`. Distinguishing fact: the BGA probe is silent only while the value is stored or compared, a total `match` is a runtime guard; here the value reaches the caller as a Present of the wrong type and the wrong `==` never matches anything, so no later match refuses it. Related rows, not duplicates: bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared (cardinality only), generic_coproduct_argument_unjudged_at_declared_return (applied argument, not Optional payload), cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing (record vs scalar literal: refused for coproducts, answers for records), a_record_accepted_where_a_declared_scalar_slot_is_declared (scalar slot, not coproduct or Optional).",

    "NATIVE v2: NOT MEASURED HERE. comparison_operands_never_judged_in_v2_infer records (C) as a v2 hole at its filing; I did not re-measure it on a native build, and I did not measure (A) or (B) in v2 either. v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance is the v2 counterpart of the seed's judgment; whether it descends the Optional payload is the open question. Do not read this row as saying v2 is clean.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silently admitted), DESIGN section 4b: values inhabit declared types. CEILING: structurally guaranteed, decidable from the declared type and the produced type at the site. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the declared-type obligation descends the Optional layer to judge the payload, and refuses a product at a declared coproduct at every position that consults it, sufficient that the four enrolled reds in `test.claim.record_escapes_declared_optional_return_witness` turn green while the two controls stay green. Operand judgment of `==` is a separate trigger, sufficient for the last two. The fix is not in this change: it edits the load-bearing infer stage and its emitted stage0 mirror and needs a whole-corpus differential (`declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel` names the instrument) before it can land. The reds are enrolled in `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` `floor_expected_red_chunk_record_escapes_declared_optional_return`.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
